WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0035: the figures' look as BG3 draws them (on top of 0001-0009, 0011-0034).

A desktop session (Gale save with Astarion): parts of the clothes black, body showing through the
clothes, less detail than in the morning. Here (wowbg3_tav.rs):
- LOD: each visual BG3 shows is drawn at its finest LOD (its LOD-0 meshes BG3 has drawn, or all of
  them before it has), not the coarser LOD BG3 picks at its default 10 m camera (0034 drew BG3's LOD:
  LOD-1 bodies, heads, hair and genitals at play distance, a coarse body bulging through the clothes).
  The palettes of all LODs of a visual are BG3's of the frame. WOW_BG3_TAV_LOD=bg3: 0034's behaviour.
- Sides: tavtex.txt flag 16 (TVT_ONE_SIDED, set by link/tools/tavtex.py from the material shader's
  RasterizerStateID) culls the back faces of the materials BG3 draws one-sided; everything was drawn
  two-sided, so the inner faces of Gale's robe showed through its front. WOW_BG3_TAV_SIDES=two: all
  two-sided as before.
- Size: plans and poses of up to 512 meshes/records (the layer's TAV_MAX; wowbg3_tav.rs MAX_MESHES, also
  wowbg3_body.rs's pose root); at 256 the Gale save with five companions (296 meshes, every LOD
  planned) did not decode, no pose fitted and every figure vanished, and the body stopped following.
The black pieces were tavtex.py's (virtual texture layers read as zeros where the tile set stops above
level 0), fixed there; vertex-colour cuts (legs in boots) are not in this patch (benilla 0010 WIP).

